      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the early 1900s brick‑making dominated the local economy until a fire destroyed the Paxton Brick Company in 1963.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paxtonville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A unique log‑style house built by Gabriel Gill in 1885 uses triple‑layer plank walls, a rare construction method for the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paxtonville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Stone American Indian arrow and spear points have been found along Middle Creek’s northern bank, hinting at prehistoric activity.",
